<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mexica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mexica were the Nahuatl-speaking people who founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-texcoco">Lake Texcoco</a> and led the Aztec Triple Alliance. They rose from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> service to dominance after defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tepanecs">Tepanecs</a> in the fifteenth century. Their warrior culture and tribute system were central to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mexica.jpg" alt="Mexica" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aztec_drums,_Florentine_Codex..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
